-- A `DrainDiags` member (`compiler/types/typecheck.mdk`), now drained.
--
-- `relay`'s inferred scheme quantifies `a` and carries both `Tweak a Int` and
-- `Tweak a Bool`.  The diagnostics-arm drain routes `relay`'s call goal through
-- `routeUndeterminedTop`, whose census sees one head tag, `Float`, for the two
-- impls.  Its single-tag arm minted the goal `Tweak Float` from that tag, dropping
-- the vector's tail, and the selector reported it `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE`.  The goal
-- is on a scheme-quantified variable, so it is the caller's and gets no route
-- from the tag.  The trees-arm drain of `run` and `build` never produced it.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER, hand-derived: `relay`'s goals belong to its callers; `main` calls it at
-- `Float`, where `Tweak Float Int` and `Tweak Float Bool` are each the unique match.
-- `relay 1 2.5` = `value 1 2.5` = `tweak True (tweak 1 (relay 0 2.5))` = 2.5, since
-- both impls return their second argument.  ACCEPT on every verb, printing `2.5`.
--
-- WHAT THIS ROW PINS: `check` must not report `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE`.  With
-- `DrainRollback` hiding the drain's diagnostics it is green either way; it is the
-- witness that must stay green when `DrainDiags` is deleted.
interface Tweak a b where
  tweak : b -> a -> a

impl Tweak Float Int where
  tweak _ x = x

impl Tweak Float Bool where
  tweak _ x = x

value : (Tweak a Int, Tweak a Bool) => Int -> a -> a
value n x = if n == 0 then x else tweak True (tweak 1 (relay (n - 1) x))

relay n x = value n x

main = println (relay 1 (2.5 : Float))
